  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on skewness, specifically preferring the lottery that is more left-skewed, meaning a greater portion of the probability is assigned to favorable outcomes. To evaluate skewness, we compare the distribution of probabilities across outcomes. Lottery A offers 3000 Euros with 90% probability and 0 Euros with 10%, so the high outcome is highly probable—this indicates strong left skewness. Lottery B offers 6000 Euros with 45% probability and 0 Euros with 55%, meaning the majority of the probability is on the zero (unfavorable) outcome—this indicates right skewness. Therefore, Lottery A is more left-skewed than Lottery B. The decision reason would prefer Lottery A. This information is derivable from the given probabilities and outcomes, so the reason can be applied.",
